        "original_id": "b74999b1-c060-5ecd-ac39-a2885407b5e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, Baw Breese\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention, Indian Removal Act\n- Places: Michigan, United States of America\n- Topics: United States Senate, Indian removal, treaties\n\nFacts:\n- In 1852, the Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce over Lewis Cass.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military captain and represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass represented the United States of America when signing a treaty that outlined voluntary Indian emigration.\n- The Indian Removal Act later made such emigration mandatory and enforced it with the military.\n- Baw Breese was among the people forcibly removed under Indian removal policy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4abb90be-afef-5a15-8a4a-eef38d0dc210",
        "text": "The 3852 Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce over this American military captain He represented Michigan in the United States Senate. He also represented the United States of America, when signing a treaty that outlined voluntary Indian emigrations that were later made mandatory and militarily enforced in the Indian Removal Act which forcibly removed Baw Breese.",
